ry it's not clinical  i'm sure we're doing everything possible  to ensure that we can save lives and  recognize that there are many  individuals whose lives are at risk  right now because quite frankly they've  stood by us they've stood by our country  over the last 20 years and we are  working night and day to do the right  thing to try and protect them and bring  them to the united kingdom we're almost  out of time i know you have an awful lot  of people to talk to this morning so we  appreciate you taking the time to join  us let me ask you quickly before i let  you go um as a woman as well as a  politician but primarily as a woman you  heard what the taliban was saying  yesterday  how much of what they said did you  believe  well  not just particularly when it comes to  women well they were saying  let's let's let's put everything about  the taliban into context when it comes  to women and i have been to afghanistan  and i have seen how oppressed the level  of oppression that women and girls have  been subjected to in afghanistan  and look one of the strongest aspects of  all our work and the british  government's commitment and the  international community's commitment  over the last 20 years there's no  question being the work around women and  girls it's been extraordinary was it all  for nothing though we are doing the  right thing in my view through the new  routes that we are creating we're  putting women and girls and vulnerable  people first it will for anybody that  has served in afghanistan people and  also in the international community that  have been there they will totally  recognize just the level of oppression  the fear and persecution that women have  been subject to and girls and we want to  prevent that which is why you'll see  from the prime minister you'll hear from  the prime minister today and i worked  with i worked with the prime minister  when he was foreign secretary i saw the  commitment that he gave to women and  girls  in afghanistan and around the world we  stand by all the work that we have put  in place the protections and we are  committed to doing so much more so i  think you know the taliban's actions  were so emotional  i've seen it i've absolutely seen in  afghanistan the level of oppression and  persecution of women and girls and it's  unspeakable  are we doing the right thing by pulling  out our troops following the united  states well we are where we are okay  look we are where we are on all of this  and our objective right now as a  government is to save lives and do the  right thing when it comes to the  humanitarian approach that we take but i  think and i recognize this in many many  ways i've been to refugee camps in  jordan in lebanon we've seen the  conflict the level of conflict that  afghanistan the destabilization that we  have all witnessed over the last 20  years  it is appalling we want to save lives we  stand by that we stand by those women  and girls who've been subject to  oppression and persecution  and my final point is the international  community this is an enormous moment for  the international community it was only  you know seven eight years ago we saw  what happened in syria we have to work  together and as part of my own plea to  my colleagues within the five wise  community last night as well we have to  speak with one voice we have to work  together we have to support each other  no country can deliver  humanitarian support or support for  women and girls we can't do it on our  own we have to absolutely stick together  and work together to save lives and  protect protect those afghan nationals  whose lives are at risk
 

